---
source: crates/biome_yaml_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: ci.yaml
---
# Input
```yaml
# should generate diagnostics
name: CI
on: push
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - run: echo "Hello"
  test:
    name: Test
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - run: echo "Hello"
  call:
    uses: ./.github/workflows/reusable.yml

```

# Diagnostics
```
ci.yaml:5:3 lint/nursery/useGithubWorkflowJobName ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This job doesn't have a name.
  
    3 │ on: push
    4 │ jobs:
  > 5 │   build:
      │   ^^^^^
    6 │     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    7 │     steps:
  
  i Without a name, GitHub shows the job ID in the workflow run and in pull request checks, which makes jobs harder to understand.
  
  i Add a name key to the job that describes what it does.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

